Add `GET /meeting/{domain}/{key}/{code}/code-check?password=…`, which works without authentication and returns the metadata (title, time, recurrence) of the meeting a join link resolves to (`404 meeting-not-found` for unknown, stale, or expired codes and for keys addressing a conversation code; `403 invalid-meeting-password` when the link is password-protected and the password query param is missing or wrong). Add `POST /meeting/{domain}/{key}/{code}/join?password=…` for authenticated users, which joins the meeting's conversation like `POST /conversations/join` via the link's code access (re-joining is a no-op) and returns the meeting with its conversation view. Both replace the pre-release `GET|POST /meeting-join?key=…&code=…` routes. Known trade-off: the optional `password` travels as a query parameter, so it can appear in access logs and browser history (nginz masks `password=` in its sanitized access log); it only gates joining a single meeting, not an account.
